From 59fe7a24da61886b510846ae1bb826bcc5cce71c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: superuser-miguel <16271056+superuser-miguel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 11:12:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Argon2: vendor PHC reference implementation (C/argon2/)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Septima encryption expansion, patch 2/N: Argon2id KDF (RFC 9106) plus
its BLAKE2b, as the memory-hard replacement for the legacy iterated
SHA-256 in 7z password derivation.

- C/argon2/: phc-winner-argon2 release 20190702, vendored VERBATIM
  (zero modifications) from the pinned tarball, sha256
  daf972a89577f8772602bf2eb38b6a3dd3d922bf5724d45e7f9589b5e830442c
  (hash matches conan-center-index's independent record).
  CC0 1.0 / Apache 2.0 dual license (LICENSE included).
  Both fill paths vendored: ref.c (portable) and opt.c (SSE/AVX);
  link exactly one — build wiring comes with the makefile patch.
- C/Util/Argon2Test/: upstream test.c (verbatim, same tarball) plus
  argon2_kat.c, self-checking RFC 9106 §5 known-answer tests
  (argon2d/i/id, full-parameter vectors with secret + AD, expected
  tags extracted from rfc-editor.org).

Validation on this branch: upstream suite passes on both fill paths;
RFC 9106 KATs pass on both fill paths; argon2id t=3 m=256MiB p=4
measures ~0.2 s (opt path, 12-thread desktop).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
